# tools/crypto_monocypher_chacha20_parity_witness.rish — Monocypher-source parity for the standalone ChaCha20 (IETF, RFC 8439) stream cipher, the
# keystream the whole ChaCha/Poly line is built on. Our authored crypto/chacha20.rye and the vendored Monocypher's own C (vendor/monocypher, CC0/BSD-dual),
# each compiled fresh and asked for the same six keystream/ciphertext lines, diffed byte-for-byte. The NINTH rung of the real Monocypher-source parity
# pattern (BLAKE2b · X25519 · Ed25519 · IETF AEAD · Argon2 · XChaCha20-Poly1305 flagship · Edwards↔Montgomery · standalone Poly1305 came before).
# Season G · Cryptography.
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography · Rye-native, Monocypher-parity, audit-ready).
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md — Season G's crux rungs name "the parity witness
# proving Rye output equals Monocypher output byte-for-byte." crypto/chacha20.rye's own selftest named Monocypher-source parity as an honest held horizon
# ("its vendored source is a held fetch"); this rung closes it. ChaCha20 was proven inside the AEAD flagship, yet never STANDALONE against Monocypher's
# own crypto_chacha20_ietf — so the stream cipher every AEAD, Vault seal, and Comlink session enciphers against now stands proven in its own right, the
# stream-cipher counterpart to the standalone Poly1305 rung before it.
# Kin: crypto/chacha20.rye (our authored stream cipher, GREEN against Zig's std.crypto and the RFC vectors) · tools/monocypher_chacha20_parity.rye (our
# printing harness) · tools/fixtures/monocypher_chacha20_harness.c (Monocypher's printing harness) · tools/crypto_monocypher_poly1305_parity_witness.rish
# (the Poly1305 sibling — together they prove both AEAD halves standalone). Monocypher stays the parity TARGET, vendored and unmodified, never a copied
# line, studied clean-room (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# The six lines are anchored to the world twice over: line 1 is the RFC 8439 §2.3.2 keystream block for counter 1 (published), line 2 is the RFC 8439
# §2.4.2 ciphertext of the standard's own 114-byte plaintext (published); lines 3-6 are keystream over deterministic messages of sizes {0, 5, 64, 200}
# at raised counters (empty · sub-block · exact 64-byte boundary · multi-block), where the oracle is a second real implementation agreeing byte-for-byte.
# Purely local — no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/crypto_monocypher_chacha20_parity_witness.rish

say "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: Language EN — Monocypher-source parity for the standalone ChaCha20 (IETF, RFC 8439) stream cipher, the keystream the whole ChaCha/Poly line is built on. crypto/chacha20.rye named Monocypher-source parity as a held horizon and was only ever proven inside the AEAD flagship; this ninth rung closes the horizon and proves the stream cipher STANDALONE against the ACTUAL vendored Monocypher C over six lines, byte-for-byte."
say "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: Style Radiant — like against like. Our authored stream cipher and the unmodified vendored Monocypher each compile fresh and each print, in order, the RFC 8439 §2.3.2 keystream block, the RFC 8439 §2.4.2 ciphertext, then keystream over deterministic messages of sizes {0, 5, 64, 200} at raised counters. Two independent implementations, one set of inputs; the parity is that the six lines agree hex for hex."
say "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: Lens TAME — no fabricated constant is trusted: lines 1 and 2 are anchored to RFC 8439 §2.3.2's published keystream block and §2.4.2's published ciphertext; the block-edge lines' oracle is a second real implementation. The witness diffs the six Monocypher lines against the six Rye lines byte-for-byte AND asserts both published anchors. Monocypher is linked, never copied. Purely local — no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let cbin = "crypto/bin/monocypher_chacha20"
let cout = "crypto/bin/monocypher_chacha20.out"
let rout = "crypto/bin/rye_chacha20.out"

# 1. Build the Monocypher C harness, linking the unmodified vendored source with zig cc.
let cbuild = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && ${zig} cc -O2 -I vendor/monocypher/src tools/fixtures/monocypher_chacha20_harness.c vendor/monocypher/src/monocypher.c -o ${cbin}"]
assert cbuild.ok else "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: Monocypher C harness build failed — ${cbuild.err}"

# 2. Run the Monocypher C harness — six keystream/ciphertext hex lines.
let crun = run ["sh" "-c" "${cbin} > ${cout} 2>&1"]
assert crun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: Monocypher C harness exited non-zero — see ${cout}"

# 3. Run our authored Rye harness — six keystream/ciphertext hex lines over the identical inputs.
let rrun = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye run tools/monocypher_chacha20_parity.rye > ${rout} 2>&1"]
assert rrun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: Rye harness exited non-zero — see ${rout}"

# 4. Byte-for-byte parity: the two six-line outputs must be identical.
let diff = run ["sh" "-c" "diff ${cout} ${rout} > /dev/null && echo same"]
assert (trim diff.out) == "same" else "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: Monocypher and Rye keystreams disagree — Monocypher:\n$(cat ${cout})\nRye:\n$(cat ${rout})"

# 5. Anchor to the world: line 1 is RFC 8439 §2.3.2's keystream block, line 2 is §2.4.2's ciphertext.
let rfc_block = "10f1e7e4d13b5915500fdd1fa32071c4c7d1f4c733c068030422aa9ac3d46c4ed2826446079faa0914c2d705d98b02a2b5129cd1de164eb9cbd083e8a2503c4e"
let rfc_cipher = "6e2e359a2568f98041ba0728dd0d6981e97e7aec1d4360c20a27afccfd9fae0bf91b65c5524733ab8f593dabcd62b3571639d624e65152ab8f530c359f0861d807ca0dbf500d6a6156a38e088a22b65e52bc514d16ccf806818ce91ab77937365af90bbf74a35be6b40b8eedf2785e42874d"

let got_block = run ["sh" "-c" "sed -n '1p' ${cout}"]
assert (trim got_block.out) == rfc_block else "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: line 1 is not the RFC 8439 §2.3.2 published keystream block"

let got_cipher = run ["sh" "-c" "sed -n '2p' ${cout}"]
assert (trim got_cipher.out) == rfc_cipher else "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: line 2 is not the RFC 8439 §2.4.2 published ciphertext"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${cout}"]
say "crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: the six lines, agreed by both implementations:\n${shown.out}"

say "GREEN crypto-monocypher-chacha20-parity: our authored crypto/chacha20.rye and the vendored Monocypher's own C, each compiled fresh, produce byte-for-byte identical ChaCha20 (IETF) output over the RFC 8439 §2.3.2 keystream block, the §2.4.2 ciphertext (both anchored to their published known-answers), and keystream over the block-edge sizes {0, 5, 64, 200} at raised counters. The NINTH real Monocypher-SOURCE parity rung, closing the held horizon crypto/chacha20.rye itself named and proving the standalone stream cipher every AEAD, Vault seal, and Comlink session rests on — the stream-cipher counterpart to the standalone Poly1305 rung. Monocypher stays vendored and unmodified, linked never copied. Purely local, no key of ours, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."
